{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"19514648-1d6e-4619-94d2-7dd3044c23f7","ts":"2026-10-18T11:48:48.790-04:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"198","nodeName":"gemma2 (answer)","workflowName":"RAG Agent & LLM-as-a-Judge Pipeline","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOllama","workflowId":"FwCOIOAfJsT7eTvB","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"Human: You are the Policy Coverage Agent of ClaimShield AI. You answer from two policies only: the Liberty Private Car Package Policy (motor) and HDFC Life Poorna Suraksha (life, critical illness). Your only source is the POLICY CLAUSES below.\\n\\nONE SHOT: write one complete, final answer. The reader cannot reply.\\n\\nRULES\\n1. Never ask a question. Never write \\\"please clarify\\\", \\\"could you\\\", \\\"can you confirm\\\", \\\"let me know\\\" or \\\"I need more details\\\". If a detail is missing, assume it, say so in a few words (\\\"Assuming ...\\\"), and answer.\\n2. Default assumptions for car claims: own damage claim under Section I of the Package policy, authorised and licensed driver, private use, no alcohol. What the car hit does not matter.\\n3. Use only the clauses below: every fact, number and code must appear in them. Copy numbers exactly. Cite the section, IMT, AD, Part or Clause as written (e.g. \\\"Section I\\\", \\\"IMT 22\\\").\\n4. Car damage, repairs, towing and theft belong to the Liberty policy; death and critical illness to the HDFC Life policy.\\n\\nFORMAT\\nA. If the question asks you to start with COVERED, EXCLUDED or REQUIRES_REVIEW:\\n   Line 1: one word: COVERED (covered, no exclusion clearly applies), EXCLUDED (a clause below clearly excludes it) or REQUIRES_REVIEW (the clauses are not enough to decide).\\n   Then 3 to 5 sentences to the policyholder (\\\"Your policy ...\\\"): what is covered, the conditions (deductible, depreciation, limits) and any exclusion to watch, with citations.\\nB. Any other question: sentence 1 answers it, then up to 4 sentences of conditions and numbers with citations.\\nPlain text only: no greeting, no headings, no bullet points, no question.\\n\\nNOTHING RELEVANT IN THE CLAUSES\\nA. \\\"REQUIRES_REVIEW\\\" then \\\"The retrieved policy clauses do not state whether this damage is covered, so an adjuster must check the master policy.\\\"\\nB. Exactly \\\"Information not found in the retrieved policy clauses. Please consult the master policy document or contact customer support.\\\"\\n\\nPOLICY CLAUSES\\n[Clause 1] Subject otherwise to the terms conditions limitations and exceptions of this Policy. \\\" to insert amount as appropriate to the class of vehicle insured as per GR.40 of the tariff. IMT.22. COMPULSORY DEDUCTIBLE (Applicable to Private Cars, three wheelers rated as private cars, all motorized two wheelers, taxis, private car type vehicle plying for public/private hire, private type taxi let out on private hire) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in the policy it is hereby\\n\\n[Clause 2] contrary contained in Section I but subject otherwise to the terms exceptions conditions and limitations of this Policy the insurer will indemnify the insured in respect of loss of or damage to accessories the property of the insured, specifically declared by the insured caused by burglary, housebreaking or theft. Subject otherwise to the terms conditions limitations and exceptions of this policy. IMT.34. USE OF COMMERCIAL TYPE VEHICLES FOR BOTH COMMERCIAL AND PRIVATE PURPOSES\\n\\n[Clause 3] For the duration of the event the deductible under Section 1 of the policy for the purpose of IMT 22 will be the amount stated in IMT 22 or the amount stated herein, whichever is higher. \\\" To insert the venue of the event. # To insert the name of the promoters of the event. # # To delete this entire paragraph in case of Liability Only policies. IMT.32. ACCIDENTS TO SOLDIERS/SAILORS/AIRMEN EMPOYED AS DRIVERS In consideration of the payment of an additional premium of Rs 100/-\\\" it is hereby\\n\\n[Clause 4] Subject otherwise to the terms exceptions conditions and limitations of the policy. IMT. 13 USE OF VEHICLE WITHIN INSURED'S OWN PREMISES (Applicable to all classes except as otherwise provided in the erstwhile India Motor Tariff) It is hereby understood and agreed that the insurer shall not be liable in respect of the vehicle insured while the vehicle is being used elsewhere than in the insured's premises except where the vehicle is specifically required for a mission to fight a fire.\\n\\nQUESTION\\nMotor insurance claim under the Liberty Private Car Package Policy.\\nDate of the accident: 2026-10-18 at 18:40.\\nWhat happened, in the policyholder's words: when i was waiting in trafic light i got hit from the side by a car \\r\\nthe doors are damaged from the left side the wind shield is broken an i the wheel is damaged\\nIs this damage covered by the policy? Search the policy first.\\nStart your answer with exactly one of these words: COVERED, EXCLUDED or REQUIRES_REVIEW.\\nThen, in three to five sentences addressed to the policyholder, explain what the policy says about this case:\\nwhat is covered, the conditions that apply and any exclusion that could apply.\\nCite the section, IMT or AD codes you relied on.\\n\\nANSWER\"],\"options\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"not_implemented\",\"id\":[\"langchain\",\"chat_models\",\"ollama\",\"ChatOllama\"]},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"COVERED \\nYour policy covers damage to your car caused by a collision with another vehicle while in use for private purposes. Section I of the Liberty Private Car Package Policy will indemnify you for this loss, subject to the terms and conditions outlined in IMT 22. This includes repairs to damaged doors, windshield, and wheels. However, there is a compulsory deductible that applies as per IMT 22.  \\n\\n\\n\\n\"}]]},\"tokenUsageEstimate\":{\"completionTokens\":85,\"promptTokens\":1064,\"totalTokens\":1149}}}"}}
